# CHANGES vs original ROBOTIS code
# ---------------------------------
# 1. Yellow road tracking for the main course. White segmentation is disabled
#    by default because the physical map has white tape that is not a lane.
# 2. Component + row-track dual extraction with quality-based deduplication.
# 3. One-lap roundabout guard: detects the roundabout/fork, counts one lap
#    from /odom yaw when available, then allows the exit pair.
# 4. Post-circle stability (FIX A):
#    - Hard center-delta gate: after exiting the circle any pair whose center
#      at lookahead deviates > POST_CIRCLE_MAX_CENTER_DELTA px from last known
#      center is rejected before scoring.  Gate is relaxed to 150 px if no
#    pair survives (avoids freezing when the lane genuinely shifts).
#    - Continuity bias / center-shift penalty cranked up so the scorer very
#      strongly prefers staying on the current pair.
#    - Switch-confirm window raised to 28 frames so transient mis-detections
#      of the adjacent parallel lane cannot cause a lane switch.
# 5. Parking straight-through (FIX B):
#    - After the required post-circle turns are counted, if a very-straight
#      pair is seen for PARKING_PAIR_REQUIRED frames the robot enters
#      ROUTE_PARKING and holds straight_hold=True.
#    - It exits parking mode when the detected pair heading rises above
#      PARKING_EXIT_HEADING_MIN (robot reaching the exit turn) and then
#      returns to normal lane follow for the final approach to the finish.
# 6. Logging: all state-change messages use rospy.logwarn so they appear in
#    roslaunch output at default verbosity.  For per-frame status use:
#      roslaunch --screen ... turtlebot3_autorace_control_lane.launch
#    or add  output="screen"  to the detect_lane node in the launch file.
################################################################################

